on entrypoint. Until a newer user message explicitly grants the source patch, keep next-decision at `hold_for_default_off_via_pole_shape_instrumentation_source_authorization` and avoid editing `src\\models\\exact_coordinate_master.py`.\n121\t- Current external review package: `...\\33_via_pole_external_review_package\\via_pole_external_review_package_001\\via_pole_external_review_package_001.zip` is built and clean-extraction validated for external review of the default-off via-pole instrumentation authorization decision. SHA256: `3c0c0e706b596c46711c6812dea70292e834fe0ace7eb37ecacac7c9cfb04bee`. The package includes S29-S32 evidence, current next-decision, review request text, and `src\\models\\exact_coordinate_master.py` as source context. It is not proof evidence and does not authorize implementation by itself. If continuing review workflow, use `docs\\coordination\\chatgpt_project_review_uploads.md` and the uploader state-tree helper to upload this exact zip and send the prepared review request.\n122\t- Current via-pole instrumentation result: after external review said the patch was safe to authorize, the user explicitly authorized the narrow default-off source patch. `EXACT_GHOST_VIA_POLE_SHAPE_INSTRUMENTATION` now defaults off in `src\\models\\exact_coordinate_master.py` and only emits `shape_instrumentation` diagnostics when explicitly set to `1/true/on`. Default-off and enabled fixture tests confirmed identical model proto text, variable count, constraint count, and constraint type distribution; `test_master.py` and `test_exact_contract.py` pass. The single allowed 42x32 enabled no-solve inventory completed at `...\\24_master_proto_inventory\\local_hotspot_42x32_master_proto_inventory_shape_inst_001\\master_proto_inventory.json` with `cp_solver_solve_called=false`, `checkpoint_written=false`, `sensitive_path_comparison.changed=false`, and no canonical checkpoint files. Result review: `...\\34_via_pole_shape_instrumentation_result_review\\via_pole_shape_instrumentation_result_review.json`, classification `instrumentation_patch_safe_but_target_loop_not_primary_wall_clock_hotspot`. Do not run more 42x32 runtime or mutate additional solver/model source until a broader no-solve overlay timing strategy is prepared and reviewed.\n123\t- Current broader overlay timing result: `...\\35_overlay_timing_strategy\\` now exists. The single wrapper-level no-solve `42x32` probe `local_hotspot_42x32_overlay_timing_probe_001` completed with no solver call, no checkpoint write, no source/model mutation, and `sensitive_path_comparison.changed=false`. Timing narrowed the model-build hotspot to coordinate ghost signature bucket tightening: `from_exact_core` about 78.53s, `_add_ghost_constraints` about 69.52s, `_apply_ghost_anchor_signature_bucket_tightening` about 66.52s, residual signature tightening about 2.22s, via-pole screen about 0.66s, search-guidance rebuild about 0.05s, and ghost anchor/interval outer residual about 0.11s. Recorded phase sum double-counts nested phases; use the per-phase hierarchy, not the raw sum. Next step is a signature-bucket tightening strategy/review artifact before any more 42x32 runtime, 67x20 retry, full-wave retry, or additional solver/model source mutation.\n124\t<!-- codex session 2026-05-02 -->\n125\t- Current signature-bucket tightening gate: `...\\36_signature_bucket_tightening_strategy\\signature_bucket_tightening_strategy.json` classifies S35 as `signature_bucket_internal_loop_strategy_required`: `_apply_ghost_anchor_signature_bucket_tightening` took about 66.52s while adding only 68 ghost-conditioned mandatory bucket constraints and 0 required-optional bucket constraints, so the suspected cost is internal payload/scanning/dedup/reduction-loop work rather than the final constraint count. `...\\37_signature_bucket_tightening_instrumentation_patch_spec\\signature_bucket_tightening_instrumentation_patch_spec.json` is spec-only and source-mutation-free; it proposes default-off instrumentation under `EXACT_GHOST_SIGNATURE_BUCKET_TIGHTENING_INSTRUMENTATION` for `CoordinateExactMasterDelegate._apply_ghost_anchor_signature_bucket_tightening` and explicitly sets `implementation_allowed_now=false`. This S37 source-patch spec still needs review first; if review passes, request explicit default-off source-patch authorization before editing `src\\models\\exact_coordinate_master.py`. Until then, do not run more `42x32` runtime, retry `67x20`, run full-wave, write checkpoints, promote proof, or mutate more solver/model source.\n126\t- Current signature-bucket external review package: `...\\38_signature_bucket_external_review_package\\signature_bucket_external_review_package_001\\signature_bucket_external_review_package_001.zip` is built and clean-extraction validated for external review of the default-off signature-bucket tightening instrumentation proposal. SHA256: `46b1287af567eb82ff6d716b47215acbb72e9f04a741f3ed70d767e087fb50f9`. The package includes S35-S37 evidence, the AGENTS review/authorization gate excerpt, `src\\models\\exact_coordinate_master.py`, S36/S37/S38 builder scripts, and focused `test_master.py` / `test_exact_contract.py` context. It is not proof evidence, not authorization, and not a source patch. Next step is external review via the ChatGPT `终末地` project review workflow; if review passes, then request explicit user/project-owner authorization before editing solver/model source. The request text sent to ChatGPT must directly name this package filename and SHA; do not rely on the reviewer inferring the target from Sources or from inside the zip.\n127\t- Current S38 external review result: the reviewer did not pass the S37 source-patch spec and explicitly said not to request user/project-owner authorization yet. Extracted reply: `.codex_test_logs\\chatgpt_project_uploader\\review_reply_extract_s38_signature_bucket_review_reply_001.md`. Blocker: the proposed instrumentation logic is scoped to `CoordinateExactMasterDelegate._apply_ghost_anchor_signature_bu